id lake. Water Res Res 19:157&#x02013;167 </citation></ref><ref id="CR32"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sundaram</surname><given-names>TR</given-names></name><name><surname>Rehm</surname><given-names>RG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The seasonal thermal structure of deep temperature lakes</article-title><source>Tellus</source><year>1973</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>157</fpage><lpage>167</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Sundaram TR, Rehm RG (1973) The seasonal thermal structure of deep temperature lakes. Tellus 25:157&#x02013;167 </citation></ref><ref id="CR33"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tibbs</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></name><name><surname>Galat</surname><given-names>DL</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The influence of river stage on endangered least terns and their fish prey in the Mississippi river (USA)</article-title><source>Regulated Rivers Res Manage</source><year>1998</year><volume>14</volume><fpage>257</fpage><lpage>266</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1002/(SICI)1099-1646(199805/06)14:3&#x0003c;257::AID-RRR500&#x0003e;3.0.CO;2-9</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Tibbs JE, Galat DL (1998) The influence of river stage on endangered least terns and their fish prey in the Mississippi river (USA). Regulated Rivers Res Manage 14:257&#x02013;266 </citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>